  "worked_solution": "To compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t,$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t)=-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(3\\operatorname{cot}\u2061t)}{-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{csc}^{2}\u2061t}{-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t} \\\\  & =3{csc}^{3}\u2061t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
